      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "The first digit broadly identifies the server class, while the final digit is typically 0 for Intel and 5 for AMD."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "Dell Australia"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "inlines": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": "Heading2",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "Practical implications for used servers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "For buying older PowerEdge hardware, I'd distinguish four platforms:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "list": {
        "key": "list1",
        "level": 0,
        "bullet": true
      },
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "12G (R720): Inexpensive DDR3 and Xeon E5 v2. PCIe 3.0. Suitable for inexpensive storage and experimentation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "list": {
        "key": "list1",
        "level": 0,
        "bullet": true
      },
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "13G (R730): DDR4 and E5 v3/v4. A useful low-cost platform, particularly where memory capacity and PCIe slots matter."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "list": {
        "key": "list1",
        "level": 0,
        "bullet": true
      },
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "14G (R740): First and second-generation Xeon Scalable, including Xeon Gold 6140. DDR4, still PCIe 3.0."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "list": {
        "key": "list1",
        "level": 0,
        "bullet": true
      },
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "15G (R750): Ice Lake Xeons, eight DDR4 memory channels per CPU versus six on 14G, and PCIe 4.0. A significant platform improvement."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "list": {
        "key": "list1",
        "level": 0,
        "bullet": true
      },
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "16G (R760): DDR5, PCIe 5.0 and substantially greater memory bandwidth."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "One particularly important distinction: a Xeon Gold 6140 is a first-generation Xeon Scalable processor, intended for 14G-class platforms, not an R720 or R730."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "style": null,
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "For a cost-sensitive GPU/inference server, 13G or 14G can still be attractive, whereas 15G becomes substantially more interesting when PCIe bandwidth or CPU-to-memory throughput matters."
        }
      ]
    }
